\section{Element order and identity}{

The aggregated list is \strong{not} in wildcard order and its elements carry no
names: \code{names()} on it is \code{NULL}. The order is the one in which the producer
instances \strong{finish}: each result is appended to the list as it arrives.

It is therefore \strong{not stable and not predictable}: it depends on how long
each instance takes, so it is neither the declared order nor the same from
one run to the next. One worker with instances of unequal duration is enough
to reorder it.

Indexing by position therefore attributes a result to the incorrect instance
\strong{silently}, with no error and a successful run: the values are real, only
assigned to the incorrect sample. To keep identity, have the producer return a
\emph{named} value (named multi-output): the names are carried with the data and
arrive aligned with it, so \code{ms[["s1"]]} is safe while \code{ms[[1]]} is not.

